From 08b4508253bffd7d71ea0be4d2f56ddfa41b1751 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 00:40:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dvbridge: a frame that is not drawn says why in the log

A Dolby Vision frame that the bridge could not draw was logged as
"render rejected stage=metadata-validation-or-reconstruction" whatever
check turned it down, and the warm-up before the first frame said only
how many of its ways of drawing failed: a report of a film that drops
to HDR10 told the stage, never the rule.

The renders of the bridge now keep why they drew nothing, a fixed text
for each check (dvbridge_render_not_drawn()), beside why the metadata
were refused (dvbridge_render_refused()): the checks of the layers, a
base layer of another bit depth than its RPU gives, libplacebo, and the
target and OpenGL of the direct way, for native output and for output
as HDR10. kodi.log says each reason once a stream, as it did for the
metadata: "a Dolby Vision frame could not be drawn: ...", "... could not
be converted for output: ...", and the warm-up names the first one
("2 could not be drawn (the first: ...)"). The same frames are drawn and
refused as before.
